title: MacSync Stealer ClickFix osascript Curl Payload Delivery
id: a8f3c2d1-7e4b-4a9f-b6c5-d12345678901
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects osascript executing shell commands that invoke curl to fetch
    attacker-controlled payloads, as observed in the MacSync Stealer
    ClickFix campaign (Microsoft Defender Experts, August 2026). Victims
    are lured via social engineering to paste malicious commands into
    Terminal, launching an interactive zsh session that uses curl to
    retrieve payloads and osascript to perform follow-on AppleScript
    activity including credential theft and data exfiltration.
references:
    - https://gbhackers.com/microsoft-links-30-domains/
    - https://cyberpress.org/macsync-stealers-30-domain-theft/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/08/19
tags:
    - attack.t1059
    - attack.t1566
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: macos
detection:
    selection_osascript_curl:
        Image|endswith: '/osascript'
        CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'curl'
            - 'http'
    selection_zsh_curl_osascript:
        Image|endswith: '/zsh'
        CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'curl'
            - 'osascript'
    condition: selection_osascript_curl or selection_zsh_curl_osascript
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate automation scripts using osascript with curl for system administration
    - Developers building AppleScript-based tools that fetch remote resources
level: high
